You're in the main branch. There are only a few branches, and they're
easily recognizable: the mines (cavelike), sokoban (lots of boulders),
the quest (get there via magic portal, you haven't gotten there yet),
etc.

> d - The most important one. After getting to AC:-7 and getting a few
> xp-levels everything seems much easier than the first 5 levels. I'm
> repeating myself "blink in the wrong moment and the game will squish
> you" but It seems I'm not advancing fast enough or something. I kill
> more and more gnomes, dwarves, etc... and nothing seems to change. I'm
> constantly satiated (hunger killed me about 1/4 of the games) and I'm
> constantly healthy. The only limitation seems to be the inventory.
> What am I doing wrong? Am I exploring too much or too slowly? (I think
> I'm xp-lvl:10 dlvl:10)

AC -7 is decent, but always keep striving for more. I don't feel
comfortable until around -20. There are still plenty of monsters that
can tear you up in just a round or two, don't think that AC -7 will
protect you from everything.

Intrinsics: do you have poison resistance? do you have magic
resistance? reflection? fire/cold/shock resistance? magic cancellation
3? I'd be seriously worrying about poison resistance at this point,
magic resistance is a very-nice-to-have and the others are less
important but still can be life savers.

Items: do you have a blessed unicorn horn? do you have holy water?
stethoscopes are nice too.

